    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The Bilinear Transform [S]\n\nA digital filter running at sample rate $f_s$ needs a transfer function in $z$. The bilinear transform substitutes\n\n$$s = 2 f_s \\, \\frac{z - 1}{z + 1}$$\n\nwhich maps the whole $j\\omega$ axis onto the unit circle, so a stable analog filter gives a stable digital one. The mapping compresses frequency, so we pre-warp the cutoff: to place the digital cutoff at $f_c$, the analog prototype uses\n\n$$\\Omega_c = 2 f_s \\tan\\!\\left(\\frac{\\pi f_c}{f_s}\\right) = 2 f_s K$$\n\nScaling the prototype by $\\Omega_c$ and substituting gives $H(z)$. The sample rate cancels, and the result depends only on $K$.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Ha : 1 / subst(s = s/(2*fs*K), butter_den(2))$\nHz : ratsimp(subst(s = 2*fs*(z - 1)/(z + 1), Ha));",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "{{K^2\\,z^2+2\\,K^2\\,z+K^2}\\over{\\left(K^2+\\sqrt{2}\\,K+1\\right)\\,z^2+\\left(2\\, K^2-2\\right)\\,z+K^2-\\sqrt{2}\\,K+1}}"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 6,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Dividing through by the leading coefficient of the denominator puts the filter in the standard form\n\n$$H(z) = \\frac{b_0 + b_1 z^{-1} + b_2 z^{-2}}{1 + a_1 z^{-1} + a_2 z^{-2}}$$",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "num_z : expand(ratnumer(Hz))$\nden_z : expand(ratdenom(Hz))$\nlead : coeff(den_z, z, 2)$\nb_sym : makelist(ratsimp(coeff(num_z, z, 2 - k) / lead), k, 0, 2)$\na_sym : makelist(ratsimp(coeff(den_z, z, 2 - k) / lead), k, 0, 2)$\n['b = b_sym, 'a = a_sym];",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ b=\\left[ {{K^2}\\over{K^2+\\sqrt{2}\\,K+1}} , {{2\\,K^2}\\over{K^2+\\sqrt{2 }\\,K+1}} , {{K^2}\\over{K^2+\\sqrt{2}\\,K+1}} \\right]  , a=\\left[ 1 , {{2\\,K^2-2 }\\over{K^2+\\sqrt{2}\\,K+1}} , {{K^2-\\sqrt{2}\\,K+1}\\over{K^2+\\sqrt{2}\\,K+1}} \\right]  \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 7,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## A 20 Hz Low-Pass at 1 kHz [S+N]\n\nFor $f_s = 1000$ Hz and $f_c = 20$ Hz we substitute $K = \\tan(\\pi f_c / f_s)$. The numerator coefficients are tiny because the cutoff is low compared with the sample rate.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "fs_v : 1000$\nfc_v : 20$\nK_v : float(tan(%pi*fc_v/fs_v))$\nb : float(subst(K = K_v, b_sym))$\na : float(subst(K = K_v, a_sym))$\nprint(\"b =\", b)$\nprint(\"a =\", a)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "b = [0.0036216815149286417,0.007243363029857283,0.0036216815149286417]\na = [1.0,-1.8226949251963083,0.8371816512560226]"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The digital response follows from evaluating $H(z)$ on the unit circle, $z = e^{2\\pi i f / f_s}$. Writing $z^{-k} = \\cos k\\theta - i \\sin k\\theta$ with $\\theta = 2\\pi f / f_s$ keeps the arithmetic real, and gives the gain and phase directly. The response matches the analog prototype at low frequencies, crosses $-3$ dB at exactly 20 Hz thanks to the pre-warping, and falls to zero at the Nyquist frequency of 500 Hz, where the bilinear transform maps $\\omega = \\infty$.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* [gain, phase] of H(z) at z = exp(i*theta), theta = 2*pi*f/fs */\nfreq_resp(f) := block([th : float(2*%pi*f/fs_v), nr, ni, dr, di],\n  nr : b[1] + b[2]*cos(th) + b[3]*cos(2*th),\n  ni : -(b[2]*sin(th) + b[3]*sin(2*th)),\n  dr : 1 + a[2]*cos(th) + a[3]*cos(2*th),\n  di : -(a[2]*sin(th) + a[3]*sin(2*th)),\n  [sqrt(nr^2 + ni^2) / sqrt(dr^2 + di^2), atan2(ni, nr) - atan2(di, dr)])$\ngain_db(f) := 20*log(first(freq_resp(f)))/log(10.0)$\n\nf_list : np_to_list(np_logspace(0, log(499.0)/log(10.0), 300))$\ndigital_db : map(gain_db, f_list)$\nanalog_db : map(lambda([f], float(-10*log(1 + (f/fc_v)^4)/log(10.0))), f_list)$\n\nprint(\"Gain at 20 Hz:\", gain_db(20), \"dB\")$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"steelblue\", line_width=2, name=\"Digital (bilinear)\", lines(f_list, digital_db),\n  color=\"darkorange\", dash=\"dash\", name=\"Analog prototype\", lines(f_list, analog_db),\n  color=\"gray\", dash=\"dot\", name=\"-3 dB\", lines([1, 499], [-3, -3]),\n  logx=true, yrange=[-100, 5],\n  title=\"Second-Order Butterworth, fc = 20 Hz, fs = 1 kHz\",\n  xlabel=\"Frequency (Hz)\", ylabel=\"Magnitude (dB)\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Gain at 20 Hz: -3.01029995663981 dB"
          ]
