    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Poles and Zeros [S+N]\n\nThe bilinear transform sends the analog zeros at infinity to $z = -1$, so this filter has a double zero there. Its two poles are a conjugate pair just inside the unit circle. They sit close to $z = 1$ because the cutoff is low, and a pole that close to the circle means a slowly decaying impulse response.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
