    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Filtering a Noisy Signal [N]\n\nThe test signal is a 5 Hz sine we want to keep, a 120 Hz interference tone we want to remove, and white noise. The filter runs the difference equation\n\n$$y_n = b_0 x_n + b_1 x_{n-1} + b_2 x_{n-2} - a_1 y_{n-1} - a_2 y_{n-2}$$\n\nsample by sample, as it would on a microcontroller.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "np_seed(42)$\nn_s : 1000$\nt_nd : np_scale(1.0/fs_v, np_arange(n_s))$\nclean : np_sin(np_scale(2*%pi*5.0, t_nd))$\nhum : np_scale(0.5, np_sin(np_scale(2*%pi*120.0, t_nd)))$\nx_nd : np_add(np_add(clean, hum), np_scale(0.2, np_randn([n_s])))$\n\niir_filter(b, a, xs) := block([ys : [], x1 : 0.0, x2 : 0.0, y1 : 0.0, y2 : 0.0, yn],\n  for xn in xs do (\n    yn : b[1]*xn + b[2]*x1 + b[3]*x2 - a[2]*y1 - a[3]*y2,\n    ys : cons(yn, ys),\n    x2 : x1, x1 : xn, y2 : y1, y1 : yn),\n  reverse(ys))$\n\nt_list : np_to_list(t_nd)$\ny_list : iir_filter(b, a, np_to_list(x_nd))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"lightgray\", name=\"Input\", lines(t_list, np_to_list(x_nd)),\n  color=\"darkorange\", dash=\"dash\", name=\"5 Hz component\", lines(t_list, np_to_list(clean)),\n  color=\"steelblue\", line_width=2, name=\"Filtered\", lines(t_list, y_list),\n  title=\"Low-Pass Filtering in the Time Domain\",\n  xlabel=\"Time (s)\", ylabel=\"Amplitude\", grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": [
