    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The filtered output tracks the 5 Hz component after a short start-up transient, with a small phase lag. Every causal IIR filter delays the signal. The phase response at 5 Hz predicts the lag:",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "phase_5 : second(freq_resp(5))$\nprint(\"Phase at 5 Hz:\", phase_5, \"rad, a delay of\", float(-phase_5/(2*%pi*5.0)*1000), \"ms\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Phase at 5 Hz: -0.36016939507891493 rad, a delay of 11.464547915445419 ms"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Checking the Attenuation with an FFT [S+N]\n\nThe design predicts how much the filter suppresses the 120 Hz tone. The FFTs of the input and output measure it. With a 1 s record each FFT bin is 1 Hz wide, so bin 120 holds the interference. We skip the first 200 ms of output, where the start-up transient sits, and compare spectra over the remaining 0.8 s.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "skip : 200$\nseg_in : np_slice(x_nd, [skip, n_s])$\nseg_out : np_slice(ndarray(y_list), [skip, n_s])$\nn_seg : n_s - skip$\nspec_in : np_to_list(np_scale(2.0/n_seg, np_abs(np_fft(seg_in))))$\nspec_out : np_to_list(np_scale(2.0/n_seg, np_abs(np_fft(seg_out))))$\nf_bins : makelist(k*fs_v/n_seg, k, 0, n_seg/2)$\nhalf(l) := makelist(l[k], k, 1, n_seg/2 + 1)$\n\nk120 : round(120*n_seg/fs_v) + 1$\nmeasured : float(20*log(spec_out[k120]/spec_in[k120])/log(10.0))$\npredicted : gain_db(120)$\nprint(\"Attenuation at 120 Hz: predicted\", predicted, \"dB, measured\", measured, \"dB\")$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"lightgray\", name=\"Input spectrum\", lines(f_bins, half(spec_in)),\n  color=\"steelblue\", line_width=2, name=\"Output spectrum\", lines(f_bins, half(spec_out)),\n  logy=true, xrange=[0, 200],\n  title=\"Spectrum Before and After Filtering\",\n  xlabel=\"Frequency (Hz)\", ylabel=\"Amplitude\", grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Attenuation at 120 Hz: predicted -31.95734101303661 dB, measured\n                                -32.05631417177529 dB"
          ]
        },
