    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Butterworth versus Chebyshev [S+N]\n\nA Chebyshev type I filter allows ripple in the passband in exchange for a steeper transition. Its squared magnitude uses the Chebyshev polynomial $T_n$:\n\n$$|H(j\\omega)|^2 = \\frac{1}{1 + \\varepsilon^2 T_n^2(\\omega)}$$\n\nWith $\\varepsilon = \\sqrt{10^{r/10} - 1}$ the passband ripples by $r$ dB. For $n = 4$:",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "T4 : expand(chebyshev_t(4, w));\nripple_db : 1.0$\neps2 : 10^(ripple_db/10) - 1$\ncheb_db(w) := float(-10*log(1 + eps2*chebyshev_t(4, w)^2)/log(10.0))$\nbutt_db(w) := float(-10*log(1 + w^8)/log(10.0))$\n\nprint(\"At 2 x cutoff: Butterworth\", butt_db(2.0), \"dB, Chebyshev\", cheb_db(2.0), \"dB\")$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"steelblue\", line_width=2, name=\"Butterworth n = 4\",\n  lines(w_list, map(butt_db, w_list)),\n  color=\"crimson\", line_width=2, name=\"Chebyshev n = 4, 1 dB ripple\",\n  lines(w_list, map(cheb_db, w_list)),\n  logx=true, yrange=[-80, 5],\n  title=\"Flat Passband or Steep Transition\",\n  xlabel=\"Normalised frequency ω/ωc\", ylabel=\"Magnitude (dB)\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "8*w^4-8*w^2+1\nAt 2 x cutoff: Butterworth -24.099331233312945 dB, Chebyshev\n                          -33.86896372610454 dB"
          ]
        },
        {
