    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "At twice the cutoff the Chebyshev filter is far deeper into its stopband than a Butterworth filter of the same order, but its passband wobbles by the 1 dB we allowed.\n\n## Summary\n\n| Step | Method |\n|------|--------|\n| Analog prototype | Symbolic: poles on the unit circle, expanded denominator |\n| Digital mapping | Symbolic: bilinear transform with pre-warping, coefficients in terms of $K$ |\n| Response and poles | Numeric: evaluation on the unit circle, `allroots` |\n| Filtering | Numeric: the difference equation, sample by sample |\n| Verification | `np_fft`: measured attenuation at 120 Hz against the design |\n\nThe symbolic derivation gives coefficient formulas that hold for any sample rate and cutoff, and the numeric half confirms the filter does what the formulas promise.",
      "metadata": {}
    }
  ]
}